WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.333
What's up everybody!

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.933
This is Emil from Pongfinity.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.466
So I was recently at the World Championships
that was held in Düsseldorf, Germany.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.866
I was invited there by the International Table
Tennis Federation, the ITTF, who wanted me

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.333
to make some trick shot videos with some of
the world's best players at the World Championships.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.466
So, well, of course I went there, I had a
great time filming with the players there

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.400
and I think the videos turned out to be really
nice.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.666
I have actually now made a compilation out
of the best trick shots we filmed there and

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.466
I think it's really nice and I'll show it
to you now.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.000
Hope you enjoy!

00:03:16.392 --> 00:03:19.032
So that was the video, it was a lot of fun
making it!

00:03:19.032 --> 00:03:23.892
Let me know in the comments below whose trick
shot do you think was the best one!

00:03:24.692 --> 00:03:30.012
I still have to say about the event itself,
the World Championships, that was absolutely

00:03:30.012 --> 00:03:36.822
amazing event, everything was so well organized
there and the venue looked incredible.

00:03:36.822 --> 00:03:41.452
I actually have a picture to show you, here's
how it looked like from inside.

00:03:41.452 --> 00:03:46.042
There were four tables in the main hall and
there were seats for 7000 or 8000 people.

00:03:46.042 --> 00:03:54.582
The atmosphere in the hall was awesome especially
during the last 3 or 4 days when it was completely

00:03:54.582 --> 00:03:56.372
sold out.

00:03:56.372 --> 00:04:00.702
As you might know, eventually most of the
medals went to the Chinese players.

00:04:00.702 --> 00:04:06.612
In the Women's singles we saw Ding Ning win
her 3rd World Championship title meanwhile

00:04:06.652 --> 00:04:11.432
in the Men's Singles Ma Long took his 2nd
World Championship title.

00:04:11.432 --> 00:04:16.172
Here's actually a picture with Ma Long after
the exhausting final.

00:04:16.172 --> 00:04:21.292
I wasn't this time able to film any trick
shots with him, but maybe some time in the

00:04:21.292 --> 00:04:23.492
future, who knows, we'll see :)

00:04:24.092 --> 00:04:28.012
But yeah, being at the World Championships
and watch some of the world's best players

00:04:28.012 --> 00:04:33.172
compete there and also film some videos with
them afterwards was an incredible experience

00:04:33.172 --> 00:04:37.452
and I just want to say huge thanks to the
ITTF for making that all possible.

00:04:38.932 --> 00:04:42.872
But I think this was all for this week's video,
if you enjoyed it please leave it a thumbs

00:04:42.872 --> 00:04:47.572
up below, and make sure to subscribe to the
channel if you haven't already!

00:04:47.572 --> 00:04:48.592
Until next time!

